1
00:00:01,135 --> 00:00:04,072
♪ In the not-too-distant
future ♪

2
00:00:04,105 --> 00:00:07,008
♪ way down in deep 13 ♪

3
00:00:07,042 --> 00:00:10,178
♪ Dr. Forrester
and TV's frank ♪

4
00:00:10,212 --> 00:00:13,380
♪ were hatching an
evil scheme ♪

5
00:00:13,413 --> 00:00:16,417
♪ they hired a temp
by the name of Mike ♪

6
00:00:16,450 --> 00:00:19,420
♪ just a regular Joe
they didn't like ♪

7
00:00:19,453 --> 00:00:22,257
♪ their experiment needed
a good test case ♪

8
00:00:22,290 --> 00:00:26,060
♪ so they conked him on the
noggin and they shot him
into space ♪

9
00:00:26,093 --> 00:00:28,897
Get me down!

10
00:00:28,930 --> 00:00:31,933
♪ We'll send him
cheesy movies ♪

11
00:00:31,967 --> 00:00:35,002
♪ the worst we can find
la la la ♪

12
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:37,938
♪ he'll have to sit
and watch them all ♪

13
00:00:37,972 --> 00:00:41,342
♪ and we'll monitor
his mind la la la ♪

14
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:44,112
♪ now keep in mind
Mike can't control ♪

15
00:00:44,145 --> 00:00:47,515
♪ where the movies
begin or end la la la ♪

16
00:00:47,548 --> 00:00:50,285
♪ he'll try to
keep his sanity ♪

17
00:00:50,318 --> 00:00:53,455
♪ with the help of
his robot friends ♪

18
00:00:55,523 --> 00:00:56,992
Robot roll call!

19
00:00:57,025 --> 00:00:58,527
♪ Cambot
[show yourself] ♪

20
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:00,027
♪ Gypsy
[I'm not ready] ♪

21
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:01,562
♪ Tom Servo
[Hello there] ♪

22
00:01:01,595 --> 00:01:03,363
♪ Crow
[that's one "o"] ♪

23
00:01:03,397 --> 00:01:06,433
♪ If you're wondering
how he eats and breathes ♪

24
00:01:06,467 --> 00:01:09,303
♪ and other science
facts la la la ♪

25
00:01:09,337 --> 00:01:12,507
♪ just repeat to yourself
it's just a show ♪

26
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:15,510
♪ I should really
just relax ♪

27
00:01:15,543 --> 00:01:20,415
♪ for "mystery science
theater 3000" ♪♪

28
00:01:34,428 --> 00:01:37,098
Hi, everybody, your local
Mike Nelson here.

29
00:01:37,132 --> 00:01:42,837
Say, listen, I've programmed
the robots to have different
regional speech patterns.

30
00:01:42,870 --> 00:01:45,940
Okay, I admit it's the only
thing I know how to do, but
still, it should be fun to try

31
00:01:45,973 --> 00:01:47,475
to watch them communicate.

32
00:01:47,508 --> 00:01:49,843
Don't you think?

33
00:01:49,877 --> 00:01:52,213
So crow, before we go to the
show, would y'all like to
have coke?

34
00:01:52,247 --> 00:01:54,548
-Sure, I'll have
a root beer.
-I said coke.

35
00:01:54,582 --> 00:01:57,118
-I know, I'll have
a root beer.
-All I have is coke.

36
00:01:57,152 --> 00:01:59,287
Then forget it,
I'll just use the bubbler.

37
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:00,488
Huh?

38
00:02:00,522 --> 00:02:01,788
Oh, by the way, what
show are we seeing?

39
00:02:01,822 --> 00:02:03,090
I thought we were
going to a movie.

40
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:04,092
We are.

41
00:02:04,125 --> 00:02:05,927
-And a show?
-No.

42
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:06,928
Then why did you say
we're going to a show?

43
00:02:06,962 --> 00:02:07,928
Because we are.

44
00:02:07,962 --> 00:02:09,297
-What show?
-"Awakenings."

45
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:10,332
That's a movie.

46
00:02:10,365 --> 00:02:11,598
I know!

47
00:02:11,632 --> 00:02:14,202
-Are you going
to come with?
-Come with what?

48
00:02:14,235 --> 00:02:15,337
Me, crow, me!

49
00:02:15,370 --> 00:02:16,603
Are you going to
come with me?

50
00:02:16,637 --> 00:02:17,905
Yeah, but I'm a little low.

51
00:02:17,938 --> 00:02:19,640
Could you borrow
me some money?

52
00:02:19,673 --> 00:02:21,508
Wait a minute, okay,
I think that's enough.

53
00:02:21,542 --> 00:02:26,413
You know, there's a difference
between regionalism and just
plain stupidity.

54
00:02:26,447 --> 00:02:28,148
But Mike, irregardless
of that fact...

55
00:02:30,252 --> 00:02:32,320
♪♪

56
00:02:33,553 --> 00:02:34,722
So what time's dinner?

57
00:02:34,755 --> 00:02:35,723
Is noon okay?

58
00:02:35,757 --> 00:02:36,757
But that's lunch!

59
00:02:36,790 --> 00:02:38,760
Lunch, dinner, same thing.

60
00:02:38,793 --> 00:02:40,962
Oh, something's flashing
over to the what's-it area.

61
00:02:40,995 --> 00:02:42,097
Ooh, the blinker!

62
00:02:42,130 --> 00:02:44,365
Ah yeah.

63
00:02:47,468 --> 00:02:48,502
Mike.

64
00:02:48,535 --> 00:02:49,503
Oh.

65
00:02:49,537 --> 00:02:50,738
What time is it?

66
00:02:50,772 --> 00:02:52,507
I slept late.

67
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:56,310
I have an experiment for
you around here somewhere.

68
00:02:56,343 --> 00:02:59,147
Frank, where's the matter
transference device?

69
00:02:59,180 --> 00:03:02,483
I didn't use it
last, Clay.

70
00:03:03,483 --> 00:03:05,453
Oh, uh, here it is.

71
00:03:05,487 --> 00:03:09,390
Well, this little device allows
you to break down molecular
patterns

72
00:03:09,423 --> 00:03:12,327
and reassemble them
again elsewhere.

73
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:14,395
I haven't gotten all the bugs
worked out of it yet.

74
00:03:14,428 --> 00:03:15,930
Thought I'd try
it out on you.

75
00:03:15,963 --> 00:03:19,567
You know, there's
a bit of an ion storm.

76
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:23,037
Are you sure you should be
sending that right now?

77
00:03:23,070 --> 00:03:24,372
Nonsense.

78
00:03:24,405 --> 00:03:27,042
What could
possibly go wrong?

79
00:03:40,322 --> 00:03:44,092
So we're not gonna do any
experiment that messes with
the laws of nature.

80
00:03:44,125 --> 00:03:48,262
You try your little matter
transference device out on
your own self.

81
00:03:48,295 --> 00:03:52,033
Yeah, you're just lucky nothing
happened sending it up there
in an ion storm.

82
00:03:52,067 --> 00:03:56,403
Oh yeah, what he said.

83
00:04:06,147 --> 00:04:07,815
What in the world?

84
00:04:07,848 --> 00:04:11,485
You failed to properly
compensate during the ion storm.

85
00:04:11,518 --> 00:04:12,987
Your agonizer, please.

86
00:04:13,020 --> 00:04:14,255
But captain Mike--

87
00:04:14,288 --> 00:04:16,457
your agonizer, please.

88
00:04:16,490 --> 00:04:17,992
Agonizer, agonize.

89
00:04:18,025 --> 00:04:19,793
Where the heck did
I put that doo-hickey?

90
00:04:19,827 --> 00:04:20,995
It's right there
on your belt.

91
00:04:21,028 --> 00:04:22,097
No, no, that's not it.

92
00:04:22,130 --> 00:04:24,032
-It is too.
-Nope.

93
00:04:24,065 --> 00:04:27,402
-I remember I had it--
-would you just give me your
agonizer, please?

94
00:04:34,375 --> 00:04:38,345
For crying out loud, you're
supposed to keep fresh batteries
in your agonizer at all times.

95
00:04:38,378 --> 00:04:41,248
-I don't know what happened,
-i-- oh, that's just great.

96
00:04:41,282 --> 00:04:42,617
Let's just go to
the agony booth.

97
00:04:42,650 --> 00:04:43,583
Please.

98
00:04:43,617 --> 00:04:44,618
It is not.

99
00:04:44,652 --> 00:04:45,953
Tom! What's happened?

100
00:04:45,987 --> 00:04:47,288
What's wrong with
Mike and crow?

101
00:04:47,322 --> 00:04:48,655
Uh, what do you mean?

102
00:04:48,688 --> 00:04:50,525
I mean, they're
all evil and stuff.

103
00:04:50,558 --> 00:04:52,493
Really?
I hadn't noticed.

104
00:04:52,527 --> 00:04:55,363
Don't you think it's just a
little weird that we're down
here in deep 13?

105
00:04:55,397 --> 00:04:56,730
That is weird.

106
00:04:56,763 --> 00:04:58,767
Still, I suppose they
do that kind of thing.

107
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:03,037
Tom, it seems as though the ion
storm sent us into an evil
parallel dimension.

108
00:05:03,070 --> 00:05:04,838
Our lives are at stake.

109
00:05:04,872 --> 00:05:06,307
We can't trust anyone.

110
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:07,842
Well, okay, let's try
to make the best of it.

111
00:05:07,875 --> 00:05:10,010
Oh, typical.

112
00:05:10,043 --> 00:05:12,180
The agony booth is
out of order.

113
00:05:12,213 --> 00:05:17,185
You can call those service
people and they'll be around,
oh, say, December, maybe.

114
00:05:17,218 --> 00:05:18,720
Well, I could
bring it out--

115
00:05:18,753 --> 00:05:20,555
shut up, yeoman crow.

116
00:05:20,588 --> 00:05:24,725
-Shutting up.
-Thank you.

117
00:05:24,758 --> 00:05:27,528
Your movie today is a little
western called "the last of the
wild horses" that I like to

118
00:05:27,562 --> 00:05:32,667
think smells like the inside
of John Goodman's chaps.

119
00:05:33,835 --> 00:05:37,172
Yippee-die-yi-yay!

120
00:05:37,205 --> 00:05:40,808
Shut up.

121
00:05:40,842 --> 00:05:45,847
And this one here is
the eight of Chris lemon...

122
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:49,217
Will you look at that?

123
00:05:49,250 --> 00:05:51,318
We've got movie sign!

124
00:05:51,352 --> 00:05:53,587
Go, go!

125
00:06:06,767 --> 00:06:08,235
[Announcer]
"Last of the wild horses."

126
00:06:08,268 --> 00:06:09,903
Aren't you going to carry
me into the theater?

127
00:06:09,937 --> 00:06:11,072
Frank, you're getting
too big for that.

128
00:06:11,105 --> 00:06:12,507
Oh, it's my favorite part.

129
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:13,808
Just watch the show.

130
00:06:13,842 --> 00:06:16,343
I have that
sciatic nerve.

131
00:06:16,377 --> 00:06:19,313
[Announcer]
This is the rogue river
valley in southern Oregon,

132
00:06:19,347 --> 00:06:23,283
-famous for its scenic
and historical landmarks.
-Like dirt and stuff.

133
00:06:23,317 --> 00:06:26,887
[Announcer] Oregon's first
settlers stopped here and built
one of the oldest settlements.

134
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:29,257
Then they moved on.

135
00:06:29,290 --> 00:06:31,292
[Announcer] ...Whose original
buildings still stand as when

136
00:06:31,325 --> 00:06:33,227
they were built nearly
a century ago.

137
00:06:33,260 --> 00:06:35,563
Wow.

138
00:06:35,597 --> 00:06:36,530
[Announcer] The entire action of
this picture was filmed in

139
00:06:36,563 --> 00:06:38,665
beautiful rogue
river valley and in

140
00:06:38,698 --> 00:06:43,737
Jacksonville, one of the few
remaining true western towns.

141
00:06:43,770 --> 00:06:47,975
So even though the
movie sucks, they still...

142
00:06:48,008 --> 00:06:49,977
Can't stress that
enough, folks.

143
00:06:50,010 --> 00:06:53,680
"Last of the wild horses."

144
00:06:55,182 --> 00:06:58,052
Frazee!

145
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:04,125
With these people and plenty
of vitamins and minerals.

146
00:07:06,293 --> 00:07:09,630
You lost the last of
the wild horses, you dink.

147
00:07:11,465 --> 00:07:15,435
Oh, Albert glasser, the man who
holds you down and pummels you
with music.

148
00:07:15,468 --> 00:07:20,040
I wonder what day Albert
glasser wrote this score.

149
00:07:21,442 --> 00:07:23,945
Two curlys fighting
for supremacy.

150
00:07:23,978 --> 00:07:25,913
I would date
yolanda molinari.

151
00:07:25,947 --> 00:07:29,083
She seems nice.

152
00:07:31,185 --> 00:07:33,453
"My life as a dog,"
the western version.

153
00:07:33,487 --> 00:07:37,558
I never wanted to do
summerstock in the first place.

154
00:07:37,592 --> 00:07:41,828
Oh yeah, the hittleman film
empire began with this movie.

155
00:07:41,862 --> 00:07:43,430
Let's save our strength.

156
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:45,533
We'll probably have to fight
later in the movie.

157
00:07:45,567 --> 00:07:49,203
-Oh.
-Oh.

158
00:07:51,938 --> 00:07:54,475
Little Joe and Adam
have it out.

159
00:07:57,912 --> 00:08:00,013
Hey, I have
leather contacts!

160
00:08:00,047 --> 00:08:02,817
You rarely see
a good facial whipping.

161
00:08:02,850 --> 00:08:04,285
...first place,
barnum.

162
00:08:04,318 --> 00:08:07,255
Now I'm going
to finish you.

163
00:08:09,190 --> 00:08:12,827
Journey to the
beginning of time!

164
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:16,630
Scrubbing bubbles, scrubbing
bubbles, ooh hoo hoo!

165
00:08:18,132 --> 00:08:19,633
Hey, he's dressed
like a cossack.

166
00:08:19,667 --> 00:08:21,968
What is that about?

167
00:08:22,002 --> 00:08:23,003
I'm not moving here.

168
00:08:23,037 --> 00:08:25,205
Look at all the people.

169
00:08:25,238 --> 00:08:27,107
Ew, smells like
grandma's purse.

170
00:08:27,140 --> 00:08:28,475
Ew.

171
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:31,278
It's the bazooka Joe guy.

172
00:08:33,013 --> 00:08:35,983
Hey, I had dibs.

173
00:08:38,385 --> 00:08:39,520
Down, down, boy.

174
00:08:39,553 --> 00:08:40,688
Shoo, go home!

175
00:08:40,722 --> 00:08:42,122
Looks like kind of
a one-sided caper.

176
00:08:42,155 --> 00:08:44,958
You're good, boss.

177
00:08:44,992 --> 00:08:46,327
Well, it's none
of my business.

178
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:49,597
I don't even know
who I am yet!

179
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:53,333
I hope it's not the three
amigos, 'cause I'd like
a comedy.

180
00:08:57,572 --> 00:09:01,608
Oh, man, a great
big juicy stagecoach!

181
00:09:01,642 --> 00:09:05,345
Oh, I'm getting horsesick.

182
00:09:08,048 --> 00:09:12,520
I hope you know that these
are billable hours, boss.

183
00:09:12,553 --> 00:09:13,988
Boss, you care
too much!

184
00:09:14,022 --> 00:09:16,290
Damn you!

185
00:09:17,792 --> 00:09:19,593
No, stay,
go home, go home.

186
00:09:19,627 --> 00:09:21,828
Go.

187
00:09:23,663 --> 00:09:24,765
Judy, freckles?

188
00:09:24,798 --> 00:09:27,067
No, go home.

189
00:09:33,773 --> 00:09:35,743
No use hanging on to that
artillery any longer.

190
00:09:35,777 --> 00:09:37,043
Might as well get
rid of it.

191
00:09:37,077 --> 00:09:38,245
See your license, please?

192
00:09:38,278 --> 00:09:39,913
I mean now.

193
00:09:39,947 --> 00:09:43,117
Oh yeah, their three guns are
probably useless against
his one.

194
00:09:43,150 --> 00:09:44,852
What are you
butting in for?

195
00:09:44,885 --> 00:09:48,088
Three against one isn't exactly
my idea of the right odds.

196
00:09:48,122 --> 00:09:51,192
I don't know who you are, but
you're not gonna get away
with this.

197
00:09:51,225 --> 00:09:53,560
I'm a bunny.

198
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:56,230
There's a law about aiding
and abetting a horse thief.

199
00:09:56,263 --> 00:09:59,200
Oh, well, now, why didn't
somebody tell me?

200
00:09:59,233 --> 00:10:01,468
Far be it for me
to break the law.

201
00:10:01,502 --> 00:10:03,303
He's being facetious,
isn't he?

202
00:10:03,337 --> 00:10:05,205
I thought he was an honest
citizen and you fellas were
breaking the law.

203
00:10:05,238 --> 00:10:07,908
Apparently sarcasm hasn't
hit the old west yet.

204
00:10:07,942 --> 00:10:10,243
I guess he must be
over the hill by now.

205
00:10:10,277 --> 00:10:12,112
No use chasing him.

206
00:10:12,145 --> 00:10:13,580
Might as well call
the whole thing off.

207
00:10:13,613 --> 00:10:18,118
-To-mah-to!
-To-may-to!

208
00:10:18,152 --> 00:10:20,722
Beep, beep, beep,
beep, beep, beep.

209
00:10:22,823 --> 00:10:24,825
Still got it.

210
00:10:24,858 --> 00:10:27,628
Vroom, vroom, vroom!

211
00:10:31,498 --> 00:10:34,468
Oh, god, that stang!

212
00:10:34,502 --> 00:10:36,103
Way to go, Ted.

213
00:10:36,137 --> 00:10:38,838
Now we have to
talk to him again.

214
00:10:38,872 --> 00:10:41,142
Please, sir, can we
have our bullets back?

215
00:10:41,175 --> 00:10:44,145
Ought to be a law against a man
carrying a concealed weapon.

216
00:10:44,178 --> 00:10:46,213
You boys get
tempted too easy.

217
00:10:46,247 --> 00:10:48,382
Get down.

218
00:10:48,415 --> 00:10:51,318
This is very awkward, 'cause
all of the horses are really
good friends.

219
00:10:51,352 --> 00:10:53,387
Very embarrassing.

220
00:10:53,420 --> 00:10:55,255
Now line dance!

221
00:10:55,288 --> 00:10:57,090
Take 'em off or
I'll burn 'em off.

222
00:10:57,123 --> 00:11:01,928
Ask him if you can show him
something in a nubuck pump.

223
00:11:01,962 --> 00:11:03,030
Let me help
you here, Gary.

224
00:11:03,063 --> 00:11:05,498
You have those hammertoes.

225
00:11:05,532 --> 00:11:10,437
Foot fetishists
of the old west.

226
00:11:10,470 --> 00:11:13,073
Now say you're gonna check
in back for a size five!

227
00:11:13,107 --> 00:11:15,910
Drop 'em!

228
00:11:15,943 --> 00:11:17,612
Did I say throw them?

229
00:11:17,645 --> 00:11:21,315
Now do it again.

230
00:11:21,348 --> 00:11:24,285
They're all wearing
white clogs.

231
00:11:26,220 --> 00:11:29,623
Hey, you've
got webbed toes.

232
00:11:29,657 --> 00:11:32,560
I miss my spur noises.

233
00:11:32,593 --> 00:11:38,598
Jacksonville, where church,
family and hopefully someday
industry come together!

234
00:11:38,632 --> 00:11:42,703
Great big backs
of the old west.

235
00:11:42,737 --> 00:11:46,173
Oh no, he just hit
a pedestrian.

236
00:11:47,942 --> 00:11:51,245
I'm so sick of
gingham I could scream!

237
00:11:52,580 --> 00:11:55,015
Ha ha, I love my job.

238
00:11:55,048 --> 00:11:56,917
We were almost held
up over near the pass.

239
00:11:56,950 --> 00:11:58,752
What do you mean, almost?

240
00:11:58,785 --> 00:12:00,120
I'm carrying
a big shipment.

241
00:12:00,153 --> 00:12:02,088
I wasn't taking
any chances.

242
00:12:02,122 --> 00:12:05,758
I was watching the road ahead
about half a mile and I seen
this masked feller.

243
00:12:05,792 --> 00:12:07,427
By the time we got around the
bend, he was gone.

244
00:12:07,460 --> 00:12:09,028
All right, we'll try
and round him up.

245
00:12:09,062 --> 00:12:10,463
Get the horses, Chuck.

246
00:12:10,497 --> 00:12:11,598
What'd he look like, Tom?

247
00:12:11,632 --> 00:12:12,800
Oh, he was a big fella.

248
00:12:12,833 --> 00:12:14,802
His own horse,
had a black bandana.

249
00:12:14,835 --> 00:12:16,237
Beautiful thighs.

250
00:12:16,270 --> 00:12:17,872
That's good enough for
me, see you later.

251
00:12:17,905 --> 00:12:18,872
Nice tummy.

252
00:12:18,905 --> 00:12:20,975
Well Mrs. Bixby
and Mrs. Jones.

253
00:12:21,008 --> 00:12:21,975
Now look, everything's
gonna be all right.

254
00:12:22,008 --> 00:12:22,977
Mrs. Bixby.

255
00:12:23,010 --> 00:12:24,345
Break it up, folks,
break it up.

256
00:12:24,378 --> 00:12:28,115
Go on home and
disappoint your husbands.

257
00:12:28,148 --> 00:12:32,018
Ew, look at
the all the poo.

258
00:12:32,052 --> 00:12:35,555
Oh, one of my
tires is low.

259
00:12:41,795 --> 00:12:45,798
I will not let you
not buy this shoe.

260
00:12:45,832 --> 00:12:49,403
Cut it out, that tickles!

261
00:12:49,437 --> 00:12:53,940
I wasn't playing
shoe store!

262
00:12:53,973 --> 00:12:58,978
His horse has the look of
someone who's spent a lot
of time humoring his master.

263
00:13:00,180 --> 00:13:01,915
-Hello there.
-Hello there!

264
00:13:01,948 --> 00:13:04,050
I just had
a little trouble.

265
00:13:04,083 --> 00:13:05,752
My horse threw a shoe.

266
00:13:05,785 --> 00:13:06,787
Ate a ringer.

267
00:13:06,820 --> 00:13:08,088
That's too bad.

268
00:13:08,122 --> 00:13:10,257
I think you can get him
reshod up at the ranch.

269
00:13:10,290 --> 00:13:11,658
Which ranch?

270
00:13:11,692 --> 00:13:13,727
-Double c.
-Oh, that's fine.

271
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:14,928
Where is it?

272
00:13:14,962 --> 00:13:15,963
What an idiot.

273
00:13:15,997 --> 00:13:17,197
You're on it.

274
00:13:17,230 --> 00:13:19,165
Covers practically
the entire valley.

275
00:13:19,198 --> 00:13:20,533
And most the world!

276
00:13:20,567 --> 00:13:22,637
Ranch house is up over
the next hill about a mile.

277
00:13:22,670 --> 00:13:24,305
Thanks.

278
00:13:24,338 --> 00:13:26,907
Say, it's lucky for me
you happened along.

279
00:13:26,940 --> 00:13:29,843
Otherwise, I might
have had to walk.

280
00:13:29,877 --> 00:13:31,778
I got news for you.

281
00:13:31,812 --> 00:13:33,280
You're still gonna walk.

282
00:13:33,313 --> 00:13:36,117
Ooh, yippee-yi-youch!

283
00:13:37,852 --> 00:13:40,220
Oh, good one, boss.

284
00:13:40,253 --> 00:13:43,590
Maybe I could just hold on to
your horse's tail and you
could drag me or someth--

285
00:13:43,623 --> 00:13:45,927
I don't know.

286
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:47,695
The double cranch?

287
00:13:47,728 --> 00:13:50,630
What is that about?

288
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:54,735
It's a sprawling studio
apartment ranch.

289
00:13:54,768 --> 00:13:57,905
What'd Jane bring
home with her now?

290
00:13:57,938 --> 00:13:59,340
How do you like
this one, dad?

291
00:13:59,373 --> 00:14:01,175
-Hello dad.
-Hello dear!

292
00:14:01,208 --> 00:14:03,343
Think you can
fix him up?

293
00:14:03,377 --> 00:14:05,312
Why, sure we can have
a shoe for his horse.

294
00:14:05,345 --> 00:14:07,080
Got more shoes
than we have horses.

295
00:14:07,113 --> 00:14:09,048
Dad's mental.

296
00:14:09,082 --> 00:14:10,717
One horse... hey, slim.

297
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:12,118
Throw a shoe on
this fella's horse.

298
00:14:12,152 --> 00:14:15,622
Thanks.

299
00:14:15,655 --> 00:14:19,327
You look like you could stand
something cool and wet.

300
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:21,428
Dad!

301
00:14:21,462 --> 00:14:23,030
So could my feet.

302
00:14:23,063 --> 00:14:25,032
Get his feet
a glass of lemonade.

303
00:14:25,065 --> 00:14:27,167
Well, don't just
stand there, go get us a drink.

304
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:30,637
Yes, dad.

305
00:14:30,670 --> 00:14:33,673
[Vocalizes]

306
00:14:33,707 --> 00:14:35,442
I like the property you
got around here.

307
00:14:35,475 --> 00:14:37,110
Real dysfunctional.

308
00:14:37,143 --> 00:14:38,512
Yeah, built it
all up myself.

309
00:14:38,545 --> 00:14:41,648
Started from scratch with
a brood of wild mares.

310
00:14:41,682 --> 00:14:44,818
Never would stop expanding
if it hadn't been for this.

311
00:14:44,852 --> 00:14:45,987
Now I'm expanded.

312
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:47,153
Ha!

313
00:14:47,187 --> 00:14:49,155
Stampede one night,
bust myself up good.

314
00:14:49,188 --> 00:14:52,425
Ever since then, I turned over
most of the management to Riley.

315
00:14:52,458 --> 00:14:53,493
That's nice.

316
00:14:53,527 --> 00:14:54,895
Where's your daughter?

317
00:14:54,928 --> 00:14:57,130
Must be a lot of wild horses
in this part of the country.

318
00:14:57,163 --> 00:15:00,067
No, no.

319
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:02,368
-His doppelganger.
-Huh.

320
00:15:02,402 --> 00:15:03,803
Trouble?

321
00:15:03,837 --> 00:15:05,305
From the small
ranch owners.

322
00:15:05,338 --> 00:15:06,840
They claim that
we're the cause of it.

323
00:15:06,873 --> 00:15:08,608
That we were taking too many
mares from the herd.

324
00:15:08,642 --> 00:15:10,577
Let them claim
whatever they want!

325
00:15:10,610 --> 00:15:13,347
Yeah! Tourettes
of the old west.

326
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:17,150
-They don't like--
-looks like you're the one that
could use something cool now.

327
00:15:17,183 --> 00:15:18,318
Hi, I'm Susan.

328
00:15:18,352 --> 00:15:21,822
I'll be your
daughter today.

329
00:15:23,123 --> 00:15:26,027
Oh, quit giving me pee.

330
00:15:29,930 --> 00:15:32,532
♪♪

331
00:15:35,135 --> 00:15:37,403
Curly and anti-curly.

332
00:15:37,437 --> 00:15:39,740
Afternoon, miss Jane.

333
00:15:39,773 --> 00:15:41,242
Mr. Cooper, Riley.

334
00:15:41,275 --> 00:15:42,843
Well, sheriff,
what brings you here?

335
00:15:42,877 --> 00:15:45,045
Oh, I'm trying to pick
up a fella's trail.

336
00:15:45,078 --> 00:15:49,048
The west palm stage just
pulled into Jacksonville
a little while ago

337
00:15:49,082 --> 00:15:52,585
and reported seeing a masked
man down near the pass.

338
00:15:52,618 --> 00:15:53,853
Sit down, sheriff.

339
00:15:53,887 --> 00:15:55,288
Thanks, Jane.

340
00:15:55,322 --> 00:15:58,558
That's a long sentence and
you're probably tried.

341
00:15:58,592 --> 00:16:00,060
Howdy.

342
00:16:00,093 --> 00:16:01,328
Stage held up?

343
00:16:01,362 --> 00:16:02,628
No.

344
00:16:02,662 --> 00:16:05,165
We had a couple extra guards
planted in the coach.

345
00:16:05,198 --> 00:16:08,535
The guard riding on the seat
was watching the road ahead
for about a half mile

346
00:16:08,568 --> 00:16:09,903
through field glasses.

347
00:16:09,937 --> 00:16:11,372
Fascinating.

348
00:16:11,405 --> 00:16:13,707
By the time they got to the
pass, the masked man had gone.

349
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:16,008
It's me!
It's me.

350
00:16:16,042 --> 00:16:19,480
I sure would have liked to have
seen the look on that fella's
face if he'd have tried to

351
00:16:19,513 --> 00:16:21,515
stick up that stage.

352
00:16:21,548 --> 00:16:25,185
The joke is on
the sheriff.

353
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:28,955
Did the guard get
a good look at him?

354
00:16:28,988 --> 00:16:30,557
Yeah.

355
00:16:30,590 --> 00:16:34,227
Good as you could a half mile
away through field glasses.

356
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:36,130
Said he was big.

357
00:16:36,163 --> 00:16:40,233
Wearing a black bandana for a
mask and riding a roan horse.

358
00:16:40,267 --> 00:16:42,903
Actually, my scarf is dark
Navy and so is my horse.

359
00:16:42,937 --> 00:16:45,372
I don't envy you
or your job, sheriff.

360
00:16:45,405 --> 00:16:49,510
This country must be full of big
fellas wearing black bandanas
and riding roan horses.

361
00:16:49,543 --> 00:16:51,010
Everyone here is so fun.

362
00:16:51,043 --> 00:16:54,415
Ah, not so many.

363
00:16:54,448 --> 00:16:57,250
Say, you got a sweet
outlaw ass, don't you?

364
00:16:57,283 --> 00:16:59,553
You're big.

365
00:16:59,587 --> 00:17:03,090
Unless I'm mistaken, that's a
black bandana you're wearing.

366
00:17:03,123 --> 00:17:05,725
They are falling
for each other hard.

367
00:17:05,758 --> 00:17:08,528
What color horse was
this man riding, Mr. Cooper?

368
00:17:08,562 --> 00:17:10,230
It was just a head
and a stick!

369
00:17:10,263 --> 00:17:11,232
It was weird!

370
00:17:11,265 --> 00:17:12,933
Roan.

371
00:17:12,967 --> 00:17:14,635
I can explain,
it was a loaner roan!

372
00:17:14,668 --> 00:17:16,270
Something's wrong, sheriff.

373
00:17:16,303 --> 00:17:18,272
I wasn't near the pass.

374
00:17:18,305 --> 00:17:21,073
I came up through
the valley.

375
00:17:21,107 --> 00:17:23,843
Let's go barefoot
all summer!

376
00:17:25,112 --> 00:17:26,313
That's just me.

377
00:17:26,347 --> 00:17:29,950
I gotta have an arch
support and a firm...

378
00:17:29,983 --> 00:17:32,652
Give me your gun.

379
00:17:32,685 --> 00:17:34,455
Well, they'll do
that sometimes.

380
00:17:34,488 --> 00:17:36,623
Well, I guess my horse
ought to be shod by now.

381
00:17:36,657 --> 00:17:38,192
-Thanks a lot, Mr. Cooper, i--
-freeze.

382
00:17:38,225 --> 00:17:39,527
Oh, they're
playing freeze tag.

383
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:41,528
What's this all
about, rocky?

384
00:17:41,562 --> 00:17:45,632
After he shot Hank, he made us
get off our horses, stampede 'em
and then took our guns.

385
00:17:45,665 --> 00:17:47,400
Took your boots
too, I see.

386
00:17:47,433 --> 00:17:50,737
Shut up, Iris.

387
00:17:50,770 --> 00:17:52,873
What have you got
to say for yourself?

388
00:17:52,907 --> 00:17:54,475
Part of what he
says is right.

389
00:17:54,508 --> 00:17:58,112
The other part
is right too.

390
00:17:58,145 --> 00:18:01,782
I just thought I'd delay them a
little and give the kid a break
when he took a shot at me.

391
00:18:01,815 --> 00:18:03,250
I'm so lost.

392
00:18:03,283 --> 00:18:05,352
...prevent anyone
from getting hurt.

393
00:18:05,385 --> 00:18:08,655
I don't like any unnecessary
gunplay going on in my
jurisdiction.

394
00:18:08,688 --> 00:18:10,957
You're gonna have to answer
to a charge of assault.

395
00:18:10,990 --> 00:18:14,562
Besides, this places you down
at the pass, which is another
little matter I want to get

396
00:18:14,595 --> 00:18:15,962
cleaned up.

397
00:18:15,995 --> 00:18:18,698
Let's go,
put it away, rocky.

398
00:18:18,732 --> 00:18:23,203
Yeah and we're gonna pin the
cattle rustling from last year
on you too if you don't mind.

399
00:18:23,237 --> 00:18:24,705
He's wearing chick jeans.

400
00:18:24,738 --> 00:18:27,073
They fit better.

401
00:18:27,107 --> 00:18:29,577
He drank our
apple juice.

402
00:18:29,610 --> 00:18:32,645
We didn't get close enough
to tell for sure.

403
00:18:32,678 --> 00:18:34,848
I suppose you took
a couple of pot shots at him.

404
00:18:34,882 --> 00:18:36,883
Well, yes, but we only tried
to put a scare into him.

405
00:18:36,917 --> 00:18:39,853
Haven't we got enough trouble
in this valley without my men
making more?

406
00:18:39,887 --> 00:18:41,588
No.

407
00:18:41,622 --> 00:18:44,257
Riley, get him out of my sight
before I have him thrown off
the ranch.

408
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:46,727
I warned you before, rocky,
about being trigger happy.

409
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:48,562
I want to talk to you.

410
00:18:48,595 --> 00:18:51,097
Glad we had this little
face-to-groin talk.

411
00:18:51,130 --> 00:18:53,433
I told you to be careful
whenever you made a move.

412
00:18:53,467 --> 00:18:56,637
Next time you go after anyone,
be sure there are no witnesses
around.

413
00:18:56,670 --> 00:18:58,138
This fella came
out of nowhere.

414
00:18:58,172 --> 00:19:00,107
Well, watch your
step from now on.

415
00:19:00,140 --> 00:19:02,675
Things are going
too good to spoil.

416
00:19:02,708 --> 00:19:04,410
I got the old man so
he won't budge.

417
00:19:04,443 --> 00:19:06,247
I put a rock
behind his wheel.

418
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:09,048
I want you to push the small
ranches around until they won't
take anymore.

419
00:19:09,082 --> 00:19:12,052
When they're pushed too far,
this whole valley will bust
loose.

420
00:19:12,085 --> 00:19:13,887
When that happens,
where do we stand?

421
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:15,288
On the sideline.

422
00:19:15,322 --> 00:19:17,323
What's a sideline, sir?

423
00:19:17,357 --> 00:19:19,827
When they do, we'll bring
the law down on them.

424
00:19:19,860 --> 00:19:22,828
And as they're wiped
out, I'll take over.

425
00:19:22,862 --> 00:19:25,932
Suppose old man Cooper's got
his own idea about all this?

426
00:19:25,965 --> 00:19:29,268
When I get through with him,
he'll see things my way or else.

427
00:19:29,302 --> 00:19:32,505
Why did they
hire hoyt axton?

428
00:19:32,538 --> 00:19:35,508
Because you got brawn where
your brains ought to be.

429
00:19:35,542 --> 00:19:38,978
You stick with me and you'll
be wearing gold bullets.

430
00:19:39,012 --> 00:19:40,247
Where?

431
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:42,248
In my belt or
in my back?

432
00:19:42,282 --> 00:19:44,885
Why, if this scene
wasn't ending, i'd--

433
00:19:44,918 --> 00:19:50,357
bless your beautiful hide
they need to invent the
stoplight.

434
00:19:50,390 --> 00:19:51,858
Remedy.

435
00:19:51,892 --> 00:19:53,160
There he is!

436
00:19:53,193 --> 00:19:55,628
Stop the music.

437
00:19:55,662 --> 00:19:57,163
Retail space for rent.

438
00:19:57,197 --> 00:19:59,833
-See?
-Hmm.

439
00:20:00,967 --> 00:20:02,502
This town has
a real western theme.

440
00:20:02,535 --> 00:20:04,170
Mmm.

441
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:08,775
I'm going to crabtree
and Evelyn.

442
00:20:08,808 --> 00:20:12,012
I'm strangely drawn--
the magnetic pull is
too strong-- oh!

443
00:20:12,045 --> 00:20:15,415
Want to go have a beer
before I book you?

444
00:20:15,448 --> 00:20:19,452
I like to greet them at the door
wearing nothing but this.

445
00:20:19,485 --> 00:20:20,720
What's the charge?

446
00:20:20,753 --> 00:20:23,423
Oh, the charge?

447
00:20:23,457 --> 00:20:25,025
Assault with
intent to kill.

448
00:20:25,058 --> 00:20:27,593
He shot Hank Davis, one
of the double c boys.

449
00:20:27,627 --> 00:20:29,663
That's right.

450
00:20:29,697 --> 00:20:32,065
Me and Terry as right there,
saw the whole thing.

451
00:20:32,098 --> 00:20:33,700
It was self-defense.

452
00:20:33,733 --> 00:20:37,237
Hank drew first and fired before
he even got his gun out.

453
00:20:37,270 --> 00:20:38,738
Hank fired four shots.

454
00:20:38,772 --> 00:20:39,907
Two.

455
00:20:39,940 --> 00:20:41,240
Sounded like four to me.

456
00:20:41,273 --> 00:20:43,110
Oh, forget it,
you weren't there.

457
00:20:43,143 --> 00:20:44,443
Having trouble
with my ears lately.

458
00:20:44,477 --> 00:20:46,947
Yeah, it's a rare ailment
known as double hearing.

459
00:20:46,980 --> 00:20:49,548
-Just like--
-you're not going to be in
this movie, are you?

460
00:20:49,582 --> 00:20:52,518
...fix up some of that
ear remedy when he gets back
to the ranch.

461
00:20:52,552 --> 00:20:55,655
We'll testify to that
at the trial, sheriff.

462
00:20:55,688 --> 00:20:57,823
Your word's all right
with me, remedy.

463
00:20:57,857 --> 00:20:59,325
Even though
you're mental.

464
00:20:59,358 --> 00:21:01,027
I guess that sort of clears you
of the shooting, doesn't it?

465
00:21:01,060 --> 00:21:02,528
Thank you.

466
00:21:02,562 --> 00:21:04,297
I'm going to hold you
on another charge.

467
00:21:04,330 --> 00:21:05,665
What kind of a charge?

468
00:21:05,698 --> 00:21:07,667
Suspicion.

469
00:21:07,700 --> 00:21:12,372
That description of the masked
man waiting to hold up the stage
fits you pretty well.

470
00:21:12,405 --> 00:21:14,007
He ain't the man you're
looking for, sheriff.

471
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:15,542
He was with us every
minute of the day.

472
00:21:15,575 --> 00:21:16,943
Wasn't he, Terry?

473
00:21:16,977 --> 00:21:18,812
Never left my sight
for a second.

474
00:21:18,845 --> 00:21:21,247
Why, he's no more a crook
than you are, sheriff.

475
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:24,450
Why, he's a new ranch hand
I hired the other day.

476
00:21:24,483 --> 00:21:27,520
Well, I guess that clears you
all the way around, doesn't it?

477
00:21:27,553 --> 00:21:30,290
It's easygoing justice
'round these here parts.

478
00:21:30,323 --> 00:21:32,892
Yep.

479
00:21:34,493 --> 00:21:36,797
Thanks, pal.

480
00:21:37,963 --> 00:21:38,932
Hey, remedy?

481
00:21:38,965 --> 00:21:40,033
Yeah?

482
00:21:40,067 --> 00:21:42,068
I want to talk
to you a minute.

483
00:21:42,102 --> 00:21:43,237
Wait a minute.

484
00:21:43,270 --> 00:21:46,540
Oh, this is gonna
be great!

485
00:21:46,573 --> 00:21:48,408
Can I show you something
in a slip-on?

486
00:21:48,442 --> 00:21:49,710
Maybe open toed?

487
00:21:49,743 --> 00:21:51,878
Something sensible,
nothing too...

488
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:55,515
I just want to remind you that
you were right here when the

489
00:21:55,548 --> 00:21:57,550
stage pulled in and
reported the whole thing.

490
00:21:57,583 --> 00:21:59,352
Me?

491
00:21:59,385 --> 00:22:02,988
You must be suffering with
that double vision I was
talking about.

492
00:22:03,022 --> 00:22:05,625
If you are, I got
a remedy for it.

493
00:22:05,658 --> 00:22:07,527
Ow, my trick nipple!

494
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:09,562
I'll tell you what
I'm willing to do.

495
00:22:09,595 --> 00:22:13,233
I'm willing to place him in your
custody until I'm satisfied one
way or the other.

496
00:22:13,267 --> 00:22:16,368
Aw, he'll come through
a third way...

497
00:22:16,402 --> 00:22:19,605
