00:42:55,340 --> 00:42:57,475
All right, men, if it's only
the herd, don't bother 'em.

997
00:42:57,508 --> 00:42:59,778
But if there's any riders,
you know what to do.

998
00:42:59,812 --> 00:43:01,480
Actually,
we don't, sir.

999
00:43:01,513 --> 00:43:04,082
Sir?

1000
00:43:04,115 --> 00:43:07,987
You see, this is where the
sepia tone really pays off.

1001
00:43:08,020 --> 00:43:10,322
Drink in the
lush photography.

1002
00:43:10,355 --> 00:43:12,758
Hey, mind your
space cushion.

1003
00:43:16,728 --> 00:43:18,730
Here they come.

1004
00:43:18,763 --> 00:43:22,902
They showed that clip at the
academy awards when that guy
was nominated for best actor.

1005
00:43:22,935 --> 00:43:26,772
On top of everything else,
they're litterers.

1006
00:43:28,473 --> 00:43:30,708
Hey, the horses
don't have guns.

1007
00:43:30,742 --> 00:43:33,078
They're quakers,
you bastards!

1008
00:43:33,112 --> 00:43:34,580
Pop, pop, pop, pop.

1009
00:43:34,613 --> 00:43:36,315
Bow, bow, bow, bow.

1010
00:43:36,348 --> 00:43:37,850
Boo-doo-daw.

1011
00:43:37,883 --> 00:43:41,687
Another Chuck and m80s.

1012
00:43:44,222 --> 00:43:45,523
Ah.

1013
00:43:45,557 --> 00:43:48,593
And then it just
sort of Peters out.

1014
00:43:49,828 --> 00:43:51,297
Spotted any of
those riders?

1015
00:43:51,330 --> 00:43:53,498
[Speaks gibberish]

1016
00:43:53,532 --> 00:43:55,033
Come on, we're going
down to the double c.

1017
00:43:55,067 --> 00:43:56,902
Wait a minute.

1018
00:43:56,935 --> 00:43:59,972
You haven't any proof it was the
double c men other than the word
of some drunk.

1019
00:44:00,005 --> 00:44:01,840
He might have just been
shooting off his mouth.

1020
00:44:01,873 --> 00:44:05,010
That's right, I'd hate to
see us make a move without
some kind of proof.

1021
00:44:05,043 --> 00:44:08,147
So would I, but-- hey, Ferguson,
look what I found in the Meadow.

1022
00:44:08,180 --> 00:44:09,815
The double c
branding iron.

1023
00:44:09,848 --> 00:44:11,117
Convinced now?

1024
00:44:11,150 --> 00:44:13,085
This settles it,
let's go.

1025
00:44:13,118 --> 00:44:16,688
So their whole plan is
based on dumb luck.

1026
00:44:19,057 --> 00:44:23,028
Whoa, Phil, you flamed
out your horse!

1027
00:44:23,062 --> 00:44:27,365
Hop sing is
making chow mein.

1028
00:44:27,398 --> 00:44:30,968
This is a gripping
Levi's commercial.

1029
00:44:31,002 --> 00:44:37,242
♪ Hi ho hi ho it's off
to work we go... ♪♪

1030
00:44:37,275 --> 00:44:38,877
We've come a-courting.

1031
00:44:38,910 --> 00:44:40,678
Delivering their
funds a-popping.

1032
00:44:40,712 --> 00:44:42,147
Hello, Mr. Ferguson.

1033
00:44:42,180 --> 00:44:43,215
We'd like to see
your father, Jane.

1034
00:44:43,248 --> 00:44:44,550
Jane? Who is it?

1035
00:44:44,583 --> 00:44:45,983
Ferguson, dad.

1036
00:44:46,017 --> 00:44:46,985
Oh, hello, Pete.

1037
00:44:47,018 --> 00:44:49,120
-Pow!
-Hello boys.

1038
00:44:49,153 --> 00:44:53,625
Old man, your picante sauce
is made in New York City!

1039
00:44:53,658 --> 00:44:54,827
I guess so.

1040
00:44:54,860 --> 00:44:56,128
Got double c on it.

1041
00:44:56,162 --> 00:44:57,930
It was found down
in the Meadow.

1042
00:44:57,963 --> 00:44:59,698
I guess one of the
boys was careless.

1043
00:44:59,732 --> 00:45:01,433
Very careless.

1044
00:45:01,467 --> 00:45:04,670
-Wow, that's like
a whole foot of ear.
-What are you driving at?

1045
00:45:04,703 --> 00:45:09,107
That iron was found down in the
Meadow after some riders drove
a band of wild horses through.

1046
00:45:09,140 --> 00:45:11,543
This is about me,
isn't it?

1047
00:45:11,577 --> 00:45:13,278
You're not insinuating
we've been raiding the herd?

1048
00:45:13,312 --> 00:45:16,682
We're not insinuating
anything, Charlie,
we're just taking facts.

1049
00:45:16,715 --> 00:45:19,618
Why, that branding iron might
have been lost a week ago,
a month ago, any time.

1050
00:45:19,652 --> 00:45:21,120
That's possible.

1051
00:45:21,153 --> 00:45:23,355
In that case, you won't object
to our looking over your stock.

1052
00:45:23,388 --> 00:45:24,523
You're darn
right I object.

1053
00:45:24,557 --> 00:45:26,258
-Wow.
-You keep out of this.

1054
00:45:26,292 --> 00:45:28,193
Sorry for lending
my support.

1055
00:45:28,227 --> 00:45:31,028
-I told you, the double c hasn't
been raiding the wild horses.
-Double cranch.

1056
00:45:31,062 --> 00:45:34,533
...won't have anybody inspect
my stock to check up on my word.

1057
00:45:34,567 --> 00:45:36,602
The whole thing's beginning
to look like a frame-up.

1058
00:45:36,635 --> 00:45:38,770
I wouldn't be surprised if one
of you fellas was backing the
whole thing in order to break up

1059
00:45:38,803 --> 00:45:40,305
the agreement.

1060
00:45:40,338 --> 00:45:41,407
If that's the way you want it,
that's all right with me.

1061
00:45:41,440 --> 00:45:42,942
You better think
this over, Mr. Cooper.

1062
00:45:42,975 --> 00:45:44,743
I have thought it over.

1063
00:45:44,777 --> 00:45:48,480
I'm giving orders any
trespassers on the double c
be shot on sight.

1064
00:45:48,513 --> 00:45:51,015
Mr. Cooper, you're only buying
yourself a lot of trouble.

1065
00:45:51,048 --> 00:45:52,417
I can pay for
anything I buy.

1066
00:45:52,450 --> 00:45:55,553
Na na na na.

1067
00:45:55,587 --> 00:45:57,222
Kindergarten baby,
wash your face in gravy,

1068
00:45:57,255 --> 00:45:59,290
wrap it up in bubblegum
and send it to the Navy.

1069
00:45:59,323 --> 00:46:01,527
Nyah.

1070
00:46:01,560 --> 00:46:03,262
Hey, come on,
I was kidding.

1071
00:46:03,295 --> 00:46:05,497
Hey, wait!

1072
00:46:05,530 --> 00:46:06,865
They still had to
pay for parking.

1073
00:46:06,898 --> 00:46:10,568
The double cranch
does not validate.

1074
00:46:12,570 --> 00:46:14,640
They've left me
no other choice.

1075
00:46:14,673 --> 00:46:16,007
Please, Jane!

1076
00:46:16,040 --> 00:46:18,543
Get the doomsday
machine!

1077
00:46:21,513 --> 00:46:23,482
-Riley.
-I wasn't listening!

1078
00:46:23,515 --> 00:46:25,417
He's the George
stephanopoulos of the ranch.

1079
00:46:25,450 --> 00:46:27,987
-Snuffleupagus?
-George snuffleupagus.

1080
00:46:28,020 --> 00:46:31,690
I've just told Pete Ferguson and
the boys that any trespassers at
the double c will be shot.

1081
00:46:31,723 --> 00:46:34,827
-[Speaks gibberish]
-Why not let the
sheriff handle it?

1082
00:46:34,860 --> 00:46:36,628
Those are orders, Riley.

1083
00:46:36,662 --> 00:46:39,497
Then if they come on your
range, you'll have the law
on your side.

1084
00:46:39,530 --> 00:46:41,132
You'll be entitled
to protection.

1085
00:46:41,165 --> 00:46:43,668
Once again,
I'm putty in your hands.

1086
00:46:43,702 --> 00:46:45,370
Over here.

1087
00:46:45,403 --> 00:46:48,140
I guess I lost my head.

1088
00:46:48,173 --> 00:46:51,910
Maybe that's the best
way to handle it.

1089
00:46:51,943 --> 00:46:55,813
John waters,
Texas ranger.

1090
00:46:55,847 --> 00:46:59,483
For a while last night,
it looked as if the whole thing
would bust wide open.

1091
00:46:59,517 --> 00:47:01,520
I had a feeling it
wasn't going to last.

1092
00:47:01,553 --> 00:47:04,757
That was a great
brunch, though.

1093
00:47:04,790 --> 00:47:07,858
Protection.

1094
00:47:07,892 --> 00:47:10,728
All right, I'll round up
some men and swear them in.

1095
00:47:10,762 --> 00:47:13,198
You won't have to
look for any deputies.

1096
00:47:13,232 --> 00:47:16,133
My rotisserie baseball.

1097
00:47:16,167 --> 00:47:17,535
Let's see.

1098
00:47:17,568 --> 00:47:18,903
"Dear sheriff, I like you,
do you like me?

1099
00:47:18,937 --> 00:47:21,840
Check one." Hmm.

1100
00:47:21,873 --> 00:47:23,375
These are all
double c men.

1101
00:47:23,408 --> 00:47:25,443
Double semen!

1102
00:47:25,477 --> 00:47:26,845
Don't touch me.

1103
00:47:26,878 --> 00:47:29,915
We're picking our
own deputies.

1104
00:47:29,948 --> 00:47:31,883
Not while I'm sheriff.

1105
00:47:31,917 --> 00:47:35,153
Wait, I'll be right up
there and then I'll retort.

1106
00:47:35,187 --> 00:47:37,388
Maybe we can do
something about that too.

1107
00:47:37,422 --> 00:47:38,990
I'd love to bite the
bridge of your nose.

1108
00:47:39,023 --> 00:47:41,827
Are you forgetting that
Cooper put you in this job?

1109
00:47:41,860 --> 00:47:43,795
Al d'amatos of
the old west.

1110
00:47:43,828 --> 00:47:46,532
Well, what's
it gonna be?

1111
00:47:46,565 --> 00:47:50,668
Our deputies or your job?

1112
00:47:50,702 --> 00:47:54,472
So, is that the end of the
scene or do you have another--
no, that's it.

1113
00:47:54,505 --> 00:47:55,740
Okay.

1114
00:47:55,773 --> 00:47:57,075
Now remember,
you're deputies.

1115
00:47:57,108 --> 00:47:58,543
What? Thank you.

1116
00:47:58,577 --> 00:48:01,580
No matter what you do,
you got the law on your side.

1117
00:48:01,613 --> 00:48:05,850
And if someone should
accidentally be killed
while resisting arrest,

1118
00:48:05,883 --> 00:48:09,487
-that's too bad.
-Huh? Huh? Get it?

1119
00:48:09,520 --> 00:48:10,688
Kill guys!

1120
00:48:10,722 --> 00:48:11,757
Can we do anything, sir?

1121
00:48:11,790 --> 00:48:13,225
Can we burn puppies?

1122
00:48:13,258 --> 00:48:15,993
Maybe this will come in handy
to settle some personal affairs?

1123
00:48:16,027 --> 00:48:18,797
Now there's a man who
understands me, thank you.

1124
00:48:18,830 --> 00:48:23,935
Now go do that voodoo
that you do so well!

1125
00:48:23,968 --> 00:48:25,370
We got the law
on our side.

1126
00:48:25,403 --> 00:48:28,040
I'm gonna fail
to yield!

1127
00:48:28,073 --> 00:48:31,277
Give it up
for my posse.

1128
00:48:32,843 --> 00:48:37,682
Guys, it's not as much fun
as I thought it would be.

1129
00:48:40,052 --> 00:48:42,753
Hey, don't push,
I'm going.

1130
00:48:44,422 --> 00:48:47,692
Now, fly,
my horsies, fly!

1131
00:48:47,725 --> 00:48:52,863
Not leaving. Just because
the rest of you are doing it,
I don't have to.

1132
00:48:52,897 --> 00:48:55,800
Let's all go to
ft. Lauderdale!

1133
00:48:55,833 --> 00:48:58,503
Ooh, blew a tire.

1134
00:49:00,172 --> 00:49:03,708
Uh, I don't think you're
supposed to burn your own barn,
Ted.

1135
00:49:03,742 --> 00:49:06,310
Well, quick cup of Joe,
then back at it.

1136
00:49:06,343 --> 00:49:08,547
[Imitates flatulence]

1137
00:49:08,580 --> 00:49:10,248
-Hey.
-It's funny.

1138
00:49:10,282 --> 00:49:12,083
What do you want here?

1139
00:49:12,117 --> 00:49:15,187
Just checking your horses to see
if there's any double c brand in
your corral.

1140
00:49:15,220 --> 00:49:16,555
Get off my place.

1141
00:49:16,588 --> 00:49:18,857
There's no double c
horses in my corral.

1142
00:49:18,890 --> 00:49:22,693
Then maybe you wouldn't mind
doing me the service of dying!

1143
00:49:22,727 --> 00:49:24,763
You're getting
double c horses now.

1144
00:49:24,797 --> 00:49:28,467
If you were alive, you'd
hear that ironic retort.

1145
00:49:28,500 --> 00:49:31,002
The tonton macoutes
of the old west.

1146
00:49:31,035 --> 00:49:35,040
Old timer,
Billy slater, no!

1147
00:49:35,073 --> 00:49:38,677
No, I don't wanna
live with grandma.

1148
00:49:38,710 --> 00:49:42,813
This guy wouldn't even be
a greeter at Roy Rogers.

1149
00:49:42,847 --> 00:49:44,950
Hey, he transmogrified.

1150
00:49:44,983 --> 00:49:47,318
He's thinner.

1151
00:49:49,788 --> 00:49:52,390
"Never liked him,"
neighbor declares.

1152
00:49:52,423 --> 00:49:54,793
Building code
invented and under fire.

1153
00:49:54,827 --> 00:49:57,395
At least there's
no art buchwald.

1154
00:50:01,365 --> 00:50:04,402
[Vocalizing]

1155
00:50:04,435 --> 00:50:06,738
Word "exonerated"
is invented.

1156
00:50:06,772 --> 00:50:10,008
Literacy rate rises
to one percent.

1157
00:50:11,375 --> 00:50:14,312
Look at that,
the orcs are involved.

1158
00:50:17,815 --> 00:50:19,517
Siamese horses!

1159
00:50:19,550 --> 00:50:24,055
-Dan Rowan and dick Martin
in "once upon a horse."
-That was a great movie.

1160
00:50:24,088 --> 00:50:27,158
Wasn't it "once upon..."
You guys, we have
the whole prairie.

1161
00:50:27,192 --> 00:50:29,895
Do we have to
bunch up like this?

1162
00:50:29,928 --> 00:50:35,067
How many of you already
know about amway?

1163
00:50:35,100 --> 00:50:36,502
Remedy and I got
word to join you.

1164
00:50:36,535 --> 00:50:39,537
[Vocalizes]

1165
00:50:42,907 --> 00:50:45,343
Howdy Hitler!

1166
00:50:45,377 --> 00:50:47,045
Go back to your homes
and ranches quietly.

1167
00:50:47,078 --> 00:50:48,480
But I live
in a trailer.

1168
00:50:48,513 --> 00:50:51,148
Who's gonna
answer for...

1169
00:50:51,182 --> 00:50:52,283
What'd he say?

1170
00:50:52,317 --> 00:50:55,787
Louder, can't
hear you back here.

1171
00:50:55,820 --> 00:50:57,922
Let the sheriff
handle the Ferguson case.

1172
00:50:57,955 --> 00:50:59,523
Mob violence
isn't the answer.

1173
00:50:59,557 --> 00:51:01,392
Who's that guy
over there?

1174
00:51:01,425 --> 00:51:03,928
We've got to tell Cooper
that he's wrong, but we've
got to do it lawfully.

1175
00:51:03,962 --> 00:51:05,997
Flop drop at ten,
pass it on.

1176
00:51:06,030 --> 00:51:08,032
How do we know you
ain't in Cooper's pay?

1177
00:51:08,065 --> 00:51:10,102
-No, I'm not in Cooper's pay.
-Don't pick at that.

1178
00:51:10,135 --> 00:51:13,972
I'm not going to stand by and
watch a range war break out if
I can possibly help it.

1179
00:51:14,005 --> 00:51:15,707
Sam, you're talking
like a fool.

1180
00:51:15,740 --> 00:51:18,042
Cooper broke
his word!

1181
00:51:18,075 --> 00:51:19,443
Pay us and we
won't kill him.

1182
00:51:19,477 --> 00:51:21,913
-Yeah.
-He might listen to me.

1183
00:51:21,947 --> 00:51:25,050
He knows I don't' own a ranch,
so I have nothing personally
to gain.

1184
00:51:25,083 --> 00:51:28,887
At least let me try before
you all do something you might
all regret.

1185
00:51:28,920 --> 00:51:30,655
Go on back to
your ranches.

1186
00:51:30,688 --> 00:51:33,225
Give me a chance to
talk to Cooper alone.

1187
00:51:33,258 --> 00:51:34,758
Yeah, I got it down...

1188
00:51:34,792 --> 00:51:36,662
Real good deal, they
were having a special.

1189
00:51:36,695 --> 00:51:38,897
You know what he's
saying is horse sense.

1190
00:51:38,930 --> 00:51:40,732
Now why don't you
all go home?

1191
00:51:40,765 --> 00:51:42,667
You see where Oklahoma
wants to be a state?

1192
00:51:42,700 --> 00:51:44,837
Can you believe that?

1193
00:51:44,870 --> 00:51:48,507
Now there are acid burns all
over this part of the prairie.

1194
00:51:48,540 --> 00:51:53,212
Wait, everybody, this means we
have to go home to our wives!

1195
00:51:53,245 --> 00:51:56,147
Look at those
horses' asses.

1196
00:51:58,583 --> 00:51:59,852
I got your message.

1197
00:51:59,885 --> 00:52:01,720
I want to see your father.

1198
00:52:01,753 --> 00:52:05,457
I hope you two
will be very happy.

1199
00:52:05,490 --> 00:52:07,592
-I only want to talk to him.
-Here's your power drill.

1200
00:52:07,625 --> 00:52:09,060
I don't think
he'll see you.

1201
00:52:09,093 --> 00:52:11,228
Somebody's gotta make him
realize what's happening.

1202
00:52:11,262 --> 00:52:13,498
The small ranchers are up
in arms over the killing.

1203
00:52:13,532 --> 00:52:15,233
So this isn't a date?

1204
00:52:15,267 --> 00:52:16,668
I'd like to help.

1205
00:52:16,702 --> 00:52:17,835
For your sake.

1206
00:52:17,868 --> 00:52:18,970
Give me time to-- no!

1207
00:52:19,003 --> 00:52:21,372
Thank you.

1208
00:52:21,405 --> 00:52:24,475
He's the Lucas
Tanner of his time.

1209
00:52:25,877 --> 00:52:27,512
Had this meeting with
a bunch of cowboys today.

1210
00:52:27,545 --> 00:52:28,813
I think it went
pretty well.

1211
00:52:28,847 --> 00:52:29,847
You should
have seen me.

1212
00:52:29,880 --> 00:52:31,583
Made me honorary chair.

1213
00:52:31,617 --> 00:52:33,452
I'm good.

1214
00:52:33,485 --> 00:52:37,688
Still needs a Billy Jack or
a Gabby Hayes or a stretch
Armstrong or something.

1215
00:52:37,722 --> 00:52:39,190
This was my idea.

1216
00:52:39,223 --> 00:52:40,725
"Flintstones: The movie."
What do you think?

1217
00:52:40,758 --> 00:52:42,593
How long you gonna
keep this up?

1218
00:52:42,627 --> 00:52:45,230
As long as they keep
stealing my horses.

1219
00:52:45,263 --> 00:52:46,865
There's a law against
that, you know.

1220
00:52:46,898 --> 00:52:49,167
There's also a law about
giving a man a fair trial.

1221
00:52:49,200 --> 00:52:50,468
No there's not.

1222
00:52:50,502 --> 00:52:52,170
And not shooting him
down in cold blood.

1223
00:52:52,203 --> 00:52:53,572
They shouldn't have
resisted arrest.

1224
00:52:53,605 --> 00:52:55,140
Resist arrest.

1225
00:52:55,173 --> 00:52:57,408
That's just an excuse
for legalized murder.

1226
00:52:57,442 --> 00:53:00,478
Pete Ferguson didn't even have
a gun on him when he resisted
arrest.

1227
00:53:00,512 --> 00:53:03,848
Just the same, there were double
c horses found in that corral.

1228
00:53:03,882 --> 00:53:06,150
I still say a man is innocent
until he's proven guilty.

1229
00:53:06,183 --> 00:53:07,418
You would think that.

1230
00:53:07,452 --> 00:53:08,453
Call off your deputies.

1231
00:53:08,487 --> 00:53:12,290
Take back your mink.

