01:04:01,905 --> 01:04:07,912
Has the defendant Duke barnum
ever threatened your father
in your presence?

1482
01:04:07,945 --> 01:04:09,880
Take the curtain,
the curtain.

1483
01:04:09,913 --> 01:04:11,348
Hey, witness, hey.

1484
01:04:11,382 --> 01:04:12,350
She's a perjur.

1485
01:04:12,383 --> 01:04:13,483
Hey, witness.

1486
01:04:13,517 --> 01:04:14,552
Yeah, no.

1487
01:04:14,585 --> 01:04:15,920
Maybe, yes.

1488
01:04:15,953 --> 01:04:16,987
Yes.

1489
01:04:17,020 --> 01:04:19,057
Oh.

1490
01:04:19,090 --> 01:04:21,325
Now he'll like me.

1491
01:04:21,358 --> 01:04:25,428
Maybe I am guilty.

1492
01:04:25,462 --> 01:04:30,067
We will now sing "a mighty
fortress is our god."

1493
01:04:30,100 --> 01:04:32,603
What is
the jury's verdict?

1494
01:04:32,637 --> 01:04:34,005
Uh, we weren't
listening, your honor.

1495
01:04:34,038 --> 01:04:36,473
Guilty, your honor.

1496
01:04:36,507 --> 01:04:42,078
Wait, they didn't say
I specifically was guilty.

1497
01:04:43,080 --> 01:04:44,482
I'm deputy dog.

1498
01:04:44,515 --> 01:04:47,117
-Hey.
-Deputy dog, hey.

1499
01:04:47,150 --> 01:04:49,787
You've been
a lousy client.

1500
01:04:52,757 --> 01:04:57,027
Here's that gun
you wan-- sorry.

1501
01:04:57,060 --> 01:05:00,530
Get going, sheriff,
get going.

1502
01:05:00,563 --> 01:05:06,203
Okay, there will be a 10-minute
break and the next sensational
trial will begin.

1503
01:05:06,237 --> 01:05:07,938
Huh?

1504
01:05:07,972 --> 01:05:10,708
12 pansy men.

1505
01:05:14,345 --> 01:05:15,312
Hey, hey!

1506
01:05:15,345 --> 01:05:17,815
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

1507
01:05:19,383 --> 01:05:21,385
That's a warehouse
in Newark.

1508
01:05:21,418 --> 01:05:24,122
Hold it, hold it, I've
always wanted to do this.

1509
01:05:24,155 --> 01:05:25,388
Ow!

1510
01:05:25,422 --> 01:05:27,558
That saved all
of two seconds.

1511
01:05:27,592 --> 01:05:29,460
Let's get him!

1512
01:05:29,493 --> 01:05:32,195
Can I get a ride
with you, Ted?

1513
01:05:32,228 --> 01:05:34,165
Ooh.

1514
01:05:34,198 --> 01:05:37,902
Oh, life is so hard
when you're stupid.

1515
01:05:40,070 --> 01:05:41,838
I wonder how that
could have happened?

1516
01:05:41,872 --> 01:05:44,942
Remedy, you're a national
friggin' treasure.

1517
01:05:44,975 --> 01:05:47,345
I wonder.

1518
01:05:49,180 --> 01:05:50,815
That's Hitchcock!

1519
01:05:50,848 --> 01:05:52,917
I want him brought in.

1520
01:05:52,950 --> 01:05:57,153
First they were mad, but
then they had to admit it was
pretty funny.

1521
01:05:57,187 --> 01:05:59,323
They should just close
this town and start over.

1522
01:05:59,357 --> 01:06:03,127
...in your mind before,
this proves that he's guilty.

1523
01:06:03,160 --> 01:06:07,565
Dr. Quinn, frontier
proctologist.

1524
01:06:07,598 --> 01:06:09,167
Isn't anybody
following me?

1525
01:06:09,200 --> 01:06:12,268
I thought I was a big
important criminal.

1526
01:06:12,302 --> 01:06:15,272
Don't know, just feels
like I forgot something.

1527
01:06:15,305 --> 01:06:19,977
Sir, why don't you put the gun
away before someone gets hurt?

1528
01:06:20,010 --> 01:06:22,345
Which was is the
territory, I wonder.

1529
01:06:22,378 --> 01:06:27,183
Well, heck, I'll just keep
going the way I was going.

1530
01:06:27,217 --> 01:06:32,357
I could have called Joel Hyatt,
but no, I go with remedy.

1531
01:06:36,427 --> 01:06:39,097
Procrastinating beaver.

1532
01:06:39,130 --> 01:06:40,998
--Duke?
Come on, Duke.

1533
01:06:41,032 --> 01:06:42,165
Have you done
your business?

1534
01:06:42,198 --> 01:06:44,868
-Did somebody
get back here?
-Duke!

1535
01:06:44,902 --> 01:06:46,037
It's remedy.

1536
01:06:46,070 --> 01:06:47,438
But kill him anyway.

1537
01:06:47,472 --> 01:06:48,972
I searched every
ranch in the valley.

1538
01:06:49,005 --> 01:06:50,540
They're headed
this way now.

1539
01:06:50,573 --> 01:06:53,010
-You got to be
moving on, Duke.
-Where to?

1540
01:06:53,043 --> 01:06:56,147
There's an old cave up in the
hills overlooking the path.

1541
01:06:56,180 --> 01:06:57,982
I used to hide there
when I was a little girl.

1542
01:06:58,015 --> 01:06:59,383
I don't think anybody
knows about it.

1543
01:06:59,417 --> 01:07:01,785
-I'll take you there.
-No, no, you better not.

1544
01:07:01,818 --> 01:07:03,853
If they should
spot me, I'd barely run around.

1545
01:07:03,887 --> 01:07:05,790
How do I get there?

1546
01:07:05,823 --> 01:07:08,625
Well, you cut across the south
end of the cuckoo ranch.

1547
01:07:08,658 --> 01:07:10,862
Wait, I'm lost,
start again.

1548
01:07:10,895 --> 01:07:13,463
-Follow that for about
a mile and then...
-Follow for a mile.

1549
01:07:13,497 --> 01:07:17,333
And then you get
shot by these guys.

1550
01:07:20,770 --> 01:07:23,973
I got a slipped disc, oh!

1551
01:07:25,508 --> 01:07:29,213
There goes the dumbest
cowboy you'll ever meet.

1552
01:07:29,247 --> 01:07:32,382
Where should
I bill you?

1553
01:07:34,185 --> 01:07:36,687
It's the night nazgul.

1554
01:07:36,720 --> 01:07:37,688
We're looking
for Duke barnum.

1555
01:07:37,722 --> 01:07:39,890
Have you seen him?

1556
01:07:52,335 --> 01:07:53,670
Okay.

1557
01:07:53,703 --> 01:07:55,572
Alternate universe manual.

1558
01:07:55,605 --> 01:07:56,773
Suppose we should
read the introduction?

1559
01:07:56,807 --> 01:07:58,142
Yeah.

1560
01:07:58,175 --> 01:08:00,812
So you die, captain,
and we all move up in rank.

1561
01:08:00,845 --> 01:08:02,078
You do not.

1562
01:08:02,112 --> 01:08:04,715
Get out of here.

1563
01:08:04,748 --> 01:08:07,485
"Welcome to the world
of alternate universes."

1564
01:08:07,518 --> 01:08:10,822
Crow has orders to
kill you, captain.

1565
01:08:10,855 --> 01:08:13,190
And he will
succeed, apparently.

1566
01:08:13,223 --> 01:08:15,893
Regrettable, but it will
leave me in command.

1567
01:08:15,927 --> 01:08:20,063
-Then I will exploit
the delithium crystal--
-Servo!

1568
01:08:20,097 --> 01:08:21,832
I can't wait to get him
back to his universe.

1569
01:08:21,865 --> 01:08:23,300
A little annoying.

1570
01:08:23,333 --> 01:08:26,003
You take a lot of chances.

1571
01:08:27,538 --> 01:08:30,073
So consider me for your
next corporate function.

1572
01:08:30,107 --> 01:08:32,810
I'm available for
all sorts of events.

1573
01:08:32,843 --> 01:08:35,478
Look, enough with
Joey the lemur.

1574
01:08:35,512 --> 01:08:39,082
Die, die, die,
die, die!

1575
01:08:39,115 --> 01:08:42,385
You know, this just might
be an alternate universe.

1576
01:08:42,418 --> 01:08:44,255
Well, duh.

1577
01:08:44,288 --> 01:08:45,890
Maybe they got
a computer down here.

1578
01:08:45,923 --> 01:08:47,157
Yeah.

1579
01:08:47,190 --> 01:08:48,992
Hey, computer?

1580
01:08:49,025 --> 01:08:50,360
[Voice]
Working.

1581
01:08:50,393 --> 01:08:51,695
Sounds like torgo!

1582
01:08:51,728 --> 01:08:52,897
[Voice]
Who?

1583
01:08:52,930 --> 01:08:53,897
Hey, computer.

1584
01:08:53,930 --> 01:08:56,233
-Working.
-Say, "the master."

1585
01:08:56,267 --> 01:08:57,500
The master.

1586
01:08:57,533 --> 01:08:59,270
That's great,
it sounds exactly like--

1587
01:08:59,303 --> 01:09:01,138
-Tom!
-Oh, right.

1588
01:09:01,172 --> 01:09:04,308
Uh, computer, are we
in an alternate universe?

1589
01:09:04,342 --> 01:09:05,308
[Voice]
Yes.

1590
01:09:05,342 --> 01:09:07,210
Well, how do
we get out?

1591
01:09:07,243 --> 01:09:11,448
[Voice] Get frank and forrester
to send back the matter
transference device.

1592
01:09:11,482 --> 01:09:14,385
-Say "the master" again.
-Belay that order.

1593
01:09:14,418 --> 01:09:16,753
Computer, would you put frank
and forrester on the screen,
please?

1594
01:09:16,787 --> 01:09:19,088
Ah, oh, right, remember,
you're the evil gypsy.

1595
01:09:19,122 --> 01:09:22,025
Oh, lord, I don't
know if I can...

1596
01:09:22,058 --> 01:09:25,362
Lord, they're still singing
that Joey the lemur song.

1597
01:09:25,395 --> 01:09:26,630
Hey, you knuckleheads.

1598
01:09:26,663 --> 01:09:28,565
Send down that matter
transference machine.

1599
01:09:28,598 --> 01:09:30,600
♪ Joey the lemur... ♪
oh, sure.

1600
01:09:30,633 --> 01:09:33,337
♪ Joey the lemur he
really is great ♪

1601
01:09:33,370 --> 01:09:36,007
♪ Joey... ♪♪

1602
01:09:37,273 --> 01:09:39,377
Ah! Wow!

1603
01:09:39,410 --> 01:09:40,978
All right, all right,
everybody here?

1604
01:09:41,012 --> 01:09:42,112
Nobody evil?

1605
01:09:42,145 --> 01:09:43,313
-Gypsy?
-Not evil.

1606
01:09:43,347 --> 01:09:45,582
I'm still not convinced
it happened.

1607
01:09:45,615 --> 01:09:47,383
Perhaps an
underdone potato,

1608
01:09:47,417 --> 01:09:49,287
or a bit of
undigested beef.

1609
01:09:49,320 --> 01:09:51,688
Let's check on the mads.

1610
01:09:51,722 --> 01:09:54,425
Oh, I feel so strange.

1611
01:09:54,458 --> 01:10:01,332
It's as if all my intestines
cried out at once and
were suddenly silenced.

1612
01:10:01,365 --> 01:10:03,233
Oh, but frank, look.

1613
01:10:03,267 --> 01:10:05,468
Someone left us
an agony booth.

1614
01:10:05,502 --> 01:10:08,805
-Me first!
-Race ya!

1615
01:10:08,838 --> 01:10:11,275
Let me in there.

1616
01:10:12,843 --> 01:10:16,013
♪♪

1617
01:10:19,550 --> 01:10:21,185
I, for one,
am glad you're back.

1618
01:10:21,218 --> 01:10:22,552
Me too.

1619
01:10:22,585 --> 01:10:25,388
What else happened?

1620
01:10:30,760 --> 01:10:34,130
Should have someone haul
away dad, I suppose.

1621
01:10:35,232 --> 01:10:36,300
Hey, it's the guy
who killed dad.

1622
01:10:36,333 --> 01:10:37,367
Yoo hoo!

1623
01:10:37,400 --> 01:10:40,803
Yoo hoo!

1624
01:10:43,607 --> 01:10:46,343
Oh, mother blood!

1625
01:10:48,312 --> 01:10:50,247
You got some of my
tapes, I think.

1626
01:10:50,280 --> 01:10:53,650
I think you got "tusk" and
"larks' tongues in aspic."

1627
01:10:53,683 --> 01:10:57,855
We got a domestic in progress
over at the old Cooper place.

1628
01:10:57,888 --> 01:11:00,390
I love you!

1629
01:11:00,423 --> 01:11:03,193
What is it about you?

1630
01:11:03,227 --> 01:11:07,063
I don't need an
answer right away.

1631
01:11:07,097 --> 01:11:10,600
Her bullets say no but
her eyes say come hither.

1632
01:11:10,633 --> 01:11:13,037
Strange courting practices
of the old west--

1633
01:11:13,070 --> 01:11:14,303
shut up.

1634
01:11:14,337 --> 01:11:17,708
So I can't use
your bathroom?

1635
01:11:17,742 --> 01:11:19,275
Jane!

1636
01:11:19,308 --> 01:11:21,178
It's me, Duke!

1637
01:11:21,212 --> 01:11:22,178
I know that.

1638
01:11:22,212 --> 01:11:23,380
Oh.

1639
01:11:23,413 --> 01:11:25,282
Stand where you are
and drop your gun.

1640
01:11:25,315 --> 01:11:26,517
But, Jane, i--

1641
01:11:26,550 --> 01:11:29,820
oh, women.

1642
01:11:32,622 --> 01:11:35,792
Jeez, I'm having
a bad day.

1643
01:11:35,825 --> 01:11:37,493
Well, that's dating
in the 90s.

1644
01:11:37,527 --> 01:11:40,963
The 1890s.

1645
01:11:40,997 --> 01:11:44,735
It's not fair,
she had a bigger gun.

1646
01:11:44,768 --> 01:11:47,303
You know what, I'm really
not that mad at him.

1647
01:11:50,740 --> 01:11:54,345
Never brides,
always bridesmaids.

1648
01:11:57,480 --> 01:11:59,850
Now he's log oggilby.

1649
01:12:02,652 --> 01:12:06,123
Everything's up to
date in Kansas City.

1650
01:12:07,792 --> 01:12:09,292
Remedy, Duke's not
at the cave.

1651
01:12:09,325 --> 01:12:11,027
It doesn't look like
he's been there either.

1652
01:12:11,060 --> 01:12:13,330
Probably couldn't
find it in the dark.

1653
01:12:13,363 --> 01:12:16,533
I think I'll get in town,
see what I can find out.

1654
01:12:16,567 --> 01:12:18,868
You sure this will
make good toilet paper?

1655
01:12:18,902 --> 01:12:21,505
If you wait till my cake
raises, I'll go too.

1656
01:12:21,538 --> 01:12:25,075
"La cage aux folles,"
western style.

1657
01:12:25,108 --> 01:12:26,110
Cid!

1658
01:12:26,143 --> 01:12:30,213
El cid! Cid!

1659
01:12:35,185 --> 01:12:37,020
Go away,
nobody likes me.

1660
01:12:37,053 --> 01:12:39,523
Emerald city is closed.

1661
01:12:42,292 --> 01:12:45,662
He's hiding in an
abandoned stuckey's.

1662
01:12:45,695 --> 01:12:49,633
This shot's just screaming
out for a huge grasshopper
to appear.

1663
01:12:49,667 --> 01:12:51,402
Everybody is so stupid.

1664
01:12:51,435 --> 01:12:55,205
He could just go into town with
a fake moustache and no one
would notice.

1665
01:12:55,238 --> 01:12:56,240
That's not my horse.

1666
01:12:56,273 --> 01:12:58,575
I'm not here, go away.

1667
01:12:58,608 --> 01:13:02,880
Lucky, this hideout is
sometimes real crowded.

1668
01:13:02,913 --> 01:13:04,380
This place is
such a mess.

1669
01:13:04,413 --> 01:13:07,517
He should clean
up his hideout.

1670
01:13:09,352 --> 01:13:10,620
You hurt bad?

1671
01:13:10,653 --> 01:13:11,855
Oh, it's not too bad.

1672
01:13:11,888 --> 01:13:12,890
Just a flesh wound.

1673
01:13:12,923 --> 01:13:13,957
Touch it.

1674
01:13:13,990 --> 01:13:16,058
Then I'll go get remedy.

1675
01:13:16,092 --> 01:13:18,228
Soon as he gets back,
we'll get you out of here.

1676
01:13:18,262 --> 01:13:19,730
I've been thinking
about that.

1677
01:13:19,763 --> 01:13:21,932
-Oh, lower.
-I want to stay here.

1678
01:13:21,965 --> 01:13:25,102
This is the last place in
the world they'd think
of looking for me.

1679
01:13:25,135 --> 01:13:27,670
He's in here!

1680
01:13:27,703 --> 01:13:28,872
Oh.

1681
01:13:28,905 --> 01:13:30,273
Yuck.

1682
01:13:30,307 --> 01:13:31,708
Stuff makes me sneeze.

1683
01:13:31,742 --> 01:13:33,143
Hay fever, I guess.

1684
01:13:33,177 --> 01:13:34,978
Remedy must have
a remedy for that.

1685
01:13:35,012 --> 01:13:37,413
We'll bring some
back for you.

1686
01:13:38,848 --> 01:13:39,983
Great scene, huh?

1687
01:13:40,017 --> 01:13:42,552
Wow.

1688
01:13:42,585 --> 01:13:47,390
This movie has more scenes of
people picking at themselves.

1689
01:13:47,423 --> 01:13:51,795
Just do a little morning bowl,
then get to work.

1690
01:13:56,900 --> 01:13:58,368
No, you can't
have any.

1691
01:13:58,402 --> 01:14:00,737
This is $80 an ounce.

1692
01:14:00,770 --> 01:14:04,073
Put a towel
under the door.

1693
01:14:04,107 --> 01:14:08,378
So you wanna walk across
the street to Fenway
and catch a game?

1694
01:14:08,412 --> 01:14:11,315
Rocky tells me that my men
are no longer deputies.

1695
01:14:11,348 --> 01:14:13,983
-Again?
-That's right, Riley.

1696
01:14:14,017 --> 01:14:16,220
The way things have quieted
down, the double c don't need

1697
01:14:16,253 --> 01:14:18,788
-any more deputies.
-Nice tobaccy aroma.

1698
01:14:18,822 --> 01:14:20,823
Is that field
and stream?

1699
01:14:20,857 --> 01:14:23,593
What about Duke barnum?

1700
01:14:23,627 --> 01:14:25,795
Oh, we can handle him
when we catch him.

1701
01:14:25,828 --> 01:14:27,297
Yep.

1702
01:14:27,330 --> 01:14:29,198
I figured my boys could
help you out there.

1703
01:14:29,232 --> 01:14:31,535
Would you stop
touching yourself there?

1704
01:14:31,568 --> 01:14:32,903
Riley.

1705
01:14:32,937 --> 01:14:34,872
This could be the start
of a beautiful friendship.

1706
01:14:34,905 --> 01:14:40,077
Duke barnum was convicted
legally and he's gonna
hang legally too.

1707
01:14:40,110 --> 01:14:42,512
But I aim to see that
he's brought in alive.

1708
01:14:42,545 --> 01:14:44,615
You pothead.

1709
01:14:44,648 --> 01:14:47,183
Go listen to some
big bamboo, huh?

1710
01:14:50,220 --> 01:14:52,255
Well, rotator
cuff feels good.

1711
01:14:52,288 --> 01:14:55,425
Think I'll be ready for
my start on Thursday.

1712
01:14:55,458 --> 01:14:56,827
Me again.

1713
01:14:56,860 --> 01:14:58,428
Where were you yesterday?

1714
01:14:58,462 --> 01:15:01,865
Brought you some
swaddling clothes.

1715
01:15:01,898 --> 01:15:04,702
A purse, thank you!

1716
01:15:04,735 --> 01:15:06,870
Wanna play
some marbles?

1717
01:15:06,903 --> 01:15:08,572
...beginning to get
on my nerves.

1718
01:15:08,605 --> 01:15:12,508
Oh, another day or two and
it'll be as good as new.

1719
01:15:14,177 --> 01:15:16,145
Ha, green sleeves.

1720
01:15:16,178 --> 01:15:18,248
Better bring me a fresh
supply of those pills.

1721
01:15:18,282 --> 01:15:20,850
I'll pick 'em up in town
tomorrow when I go for my mail.

1722
01:15:20,883 --> 01:15:22,920
What's been going on?

1723
01:15:22,953 --> 01:15:25,488
Well, this Cooper thing sort of
put an end to all that fighting.

1724
01:15:25,522 --> 01:15:28,725
The coy remedy.

1725
01:15:28,758 --> 01:15:31,495
Let's fill the canteen
with brown mustard.

1726
01:15:31,528 --> 01:15:33,297
Funny thing happened
the other morning.

1727
01:15:33,330 --> 01:15:35,698
A priest and
a rabbi walk-- oh.

1728
01:15:35,732 --> 01:15:39,703
